    "description": "",
    "in": "query",
    "name": "date",
    "required": false,
    "schema": {
      "description": "A trading date in the format of YYYY-MM-DD.\nThis is optional and by default the last trading date.\n",
      "example": "2024-01-18",
      "title": "Optional Market Date",
      "type": "string"
    }
  }
]

```

## GET /api/stock/{ticker}/volatility/option-sentiment

Per-ticker options positioning sentiment (and recent history): VWKS (volume-weighted strike-spot
"center of volume mass") and AVAR (call vs put IV asymmetry), blended into a bullish/bearish score.
Positive = bullish positioning (volume above spot, calls bid up); negative = bearish.


```json
[
  {
    "description": "",
    "in": "query",
    "name": "date",
    "required": false,
    "schema": {
      "description": "A trading date in the format of YYYY-MM-DD.\nThis is optional and by default the last trading date.\n",
      "example": "2024-01-18",
      "title": "Optional Market Date",
      "type": "string"
    }
  }
]

```

## GET /api/stock/{ticker}/volatility/realized

Returns implied and realized volatility history for a ticker. `days` selects the realized volatility
horizon in trading days. Each realized horizon uses its mapped implied volatility horizon. The default
is 21 trading days of realized volatility paired with 30 calendar days of implied volatility.

A row's `date` is the implied volatility observation date. `unshifted_rv_date` is the date when the
realized volatility window ends. Recent rows can have a `null` realized value until that window ends.


```json
[
  {
    "description": "",
    "in": "query",
    "name": "date",
    "required": false,
    "schema": {
      "description": "A trading date in the format of YYYY-MM-DD.\nThis is optional and by default the last trading date.\n",
      "example": "2024-01-18",
      "title": "Optional Market Date",
      "type": "string"
    }
  },
  {
    "description": "",
    "in": "query",
    "name": "timeframe",
    "required": false,
    "schema": {
      "default": "1Y",
      "description": "The timeframe of the data to return.\nCan be one of the following formats:\n- YTD\n- 1D, 2D, etc.\n- 1W, 2W, etc.\n- 1M, 2M, etc.\n- 1Y, 2Y, etc.\n",
      "example": "2M",
      "title": "Time frame",
      "type": "string"
    }
  }
]

```

## GET /api/stock/{ticker}/volatility/realized/windows

Returns every realized volatility horizon with a completion date in the requested calendar lookback.
`history_days` defaults to 365 and cannot exceed 365. Rows are ordered by completion date from newest to oldest.


```json
[
  {
    "description": "",
    "in": "query",
    "name": "date",
    "required": false,
    "schema": {
      "description": "A trading date in the format of YYYY-MM-DD.\nThis is optional and by default the last trading date.\n",
      "example": "2024-01-18",
      "title": "Optional Market Date",
      "type": "string"
    }
  }
]

```

## GET /api/stock/{ticker}/volatility/stats

Returns comprehensive volatility statistics for a ticker on a specific date, including
implied volatility data, realized volatility data, and their respective high/low values
for the past year.


```json
[
  {
    "description": "",
    "in": "query",
    "name": "date",
    "required": false,
    "schema": {
      "description": "A trading date in the format of YYYY-MM-DD.\nThis is optional and by default the last trading date.\n",
      "example": "2024-01-18",
      "title": "Optional Market Date",
      "type": "string"
    }
  }
]

```

## GET /api/stock/{ticker}/volatility/term-structure

The average of the latest volatilities for the at the money call and put contracts for every expiry date.


```json
[
  {
    "description": "",
    "in": "query",
    "name": "date",
    "required": false,
    "schema": {
      "description": "A trading date in the format of YYYY-MM-DD.\nThis is optional and by default the last trading date.\n",
      "example": "2024-01-18",
      "title": "Optional Market Date",
      "type": "string"
    }
  }
]

```

## GET /api/stock/{ticker}/volatility/term-structure/distribution

Returns one row per expiry with the range of that expiry's at the money implied volatility over the
365 calendar days ending on `date`. Each row holds the minimum, first quartile, median, third quartile
and maximum of the daily values, the value on `date`, and the share of daily values at or below it.

The response covers expiries after `date` and at most 365 days after it. An expiry without a value on
`date` is omitted. Expiries listed recently have few daily values, so check `samples` before comparing
ranges. Rows are ordered by expiry from nearest to furthest. `date` defaults to the last trading day.


```json
[
  {
    "description": "",
    "in": "query",
    "name": "date",
    "required": false,
    "schema": {
      "description": "A trading date in the format of YYYY-MM-DD.\nThis is optional and by default the last trading date.\n",
      "example": "2024-01-18",
      "title": "Optional Market Date",
      "type": "string"
    }
  }
]

```

## GET /api/stock/{ticker}/volatility/variance-risk-premium

Returns variance risk premium history for a ticker. `days` selects the realized volatility horizon in
trading days. The default is 21 trading days paired with 30 calendar days of implied volatility.


```json
[
  {
    "description": "",
    "in": "query",
    "name": "date",
    "required": false,
    "schema": {
      "description": "A trading date in the format of YYYY-MM-DD.\nThis is optional and by default the last trading date.\n",
      "example": "2024-01-18",
      "title": "Optional Market Date",
      "type": "string"
    }
  }
]

```

## GET /api/stock/{ticker}/volatility/variance-risk-premium/windows

Returns every variance risk premium horizon with an implied volatility observation date in the requested
calendar lookback. `history_days` defaults to 365 and cannot exceed 365. Rows are ordered by observation
date from newest to oldest. Each row includes the realized volatility completion date.


```json
[
  {
    "description": "",
    "in": "query",
    "name": "date",
    "required": false,
    "schema": {
      "description": "A trading date in the format of YYYY-MM-DD.\nThis is optional and by default the last trading date.\n",
      "example": "2024-01-18",
      "title": "Optional Market Date",
      "type": "string"
    }
  }
]

```

## GET /api/volatility/anomaly/top

Screener of the top volatility anomalies on a date, by `direction` (`short_vol` or `long_vol`).
Supports the same filters as the website screener.

This is a point-in-time screen queryable by date and includes the full component fields. History is
limited to roughly the last three to four weeks.


```json
[
  {
    "description": "",
    "in": "query",
    "name": "date",
    "required": false,
    "schema": {
      "description": "A trading date in the format of YYYY-MM-DD.\nThis is optional and by default the last trading date.\n",
      "example": "2024-01-18",
      "title": "Optional Market Date",
      "type": "string"
    }
  },
  {
    "description": "Max rows (default 50, max 200).",
    "in": "query",
    "name": "limit",
    "required": false,
    "schema": {
      "type": "integer"
    }
  }
]

```

